            <ArticleTitle>Salvage of failed Sauvé-Kapandji procedure with an ulnar head prosthesis: report of three cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>271-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three failed Sauvé-Kapandji procedures were salvaged using an ulnar head prosthesis. At 7-22 month follow-up, all three patients were much improved. However, the stem of one implant subsequently fractured in a fall and this implant had to be removed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
